                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "49ec12ac-f951-46ec-bf55-aa545c171dd6",
                        "source_entry_id": "a8bfc4a8-4fda-361c-a65f-2aae0ce0f648",
                        "source_sense_id": "c7becfc9-a454-39ee-8f59-6531b7f0418a",
                        "target_lang_word": "coordination",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "coordination",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4b29ff9e-b711-3e30-b917-28dd187b1cca",
                                        "entry_id": "00bee926-f1f2-3e01-908a-83f4b04bd73a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The act of coordinating, making different people or things work together for a goal or effect."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0757d8ac-649a-4b7c-b807-57071d47f0fb",
                                                "sense_id": "4b29ff9e-b711-3e30-b917-28dd187b1cca",
                                                "text": "Then there's the State Service and the police and several other services. And there is no proper co-ordination, no single head for all these agencies."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d58c0507-4d54-3bee-9f5b-03abbc2a6a04",
                                        "entry_id": "00bee926-f1f2-3e01-908a-83f4b04bd73a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The resulting state of working together; cooperation; synchronization."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ad33c02e-2d5c-4a94-b805-a9f65bdb5cf2",
                                                "sense_id": "d58c0507-4d54-3bee-9f5b-03abbc2a6a04",
                                                "text": "We stood dodging each other a moment with that unfortunate co-ordination of purpose men sometimes encounter when passing each other."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "93d9a877-56ac-3078-a6af-df0bccca26de",
                                        "entry_id": "00bee926-f1f2-3e01-908a-83f4b04bd73a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The ability to coordinate one's senses and physical movements in order to act skillfully."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "822b4587-9ab8-41ea-b6b6-1043656b9ef6",
                                                "sense_id": "93d9a877-56ac-3078-a6af-df0bccca26de",
                                                "text": "I’m terrible at sports; I have no coordination."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "62532605-2c29-39a8-9b3f-7e3de2de7225",
                                        "entry_id": "00bee926-f1f2-3e01-908a-83f4b04bd73a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being equal in rank or power."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e64d2f87-85ab-4c5f-9ff0-67185e050f3f",
                                                "sense_id": "62532605-2c29-39a8-9b3f-7e3de2de7225",
                                                "text": "There are two possible modes of unity in a State; one by absolute co-ordination of each to all, and of all to each; the other by subordination of classes and offices."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "43bd2291-775e-34d2-94c3-8dcfdeb8c827",
                                        "entry_id": "00bee926-f1f2-3e01-908a-83f4b04bd73a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An equal joining together of two or more phrases or clauses, for example, using and, or, or but."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d965ee4b-b475-4944-b14f-e2340bf91820",
                                                "sense_id": "43bd2291-775e-34d2-94c3-8dcfdeb8c827",
                                                "text": "There’s a wealth of other complex facts about coordination that could be explored […] coordinations with but are limited to two coordinates […]; yet coordinations with and or with or can have any number of coordinates, with the coordinator preceding just the last one […] or repeated before all except the first […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa5949aa-14ef-3518-b3fa-c72c2c439971",
                                        "entry_id": "00bee926-f1f2-3e01-908a-83f4b04bd73a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The reaction of one or more ligands with a metal ion to form a coordination compound."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5d561aae-f767-4f99-8283-f00a7be2ed3b",
